From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:19:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] DSMod: stage and load native modules on Windows

Move module staging out of mod_module.cpp into mod_module_stage.{h,cpp}
(std + POSIX/Win32 only) and add a Windows branch:

- Platform() reports windows-x86_64 on x64 Windows (_M_X64 or __x86_64__).
- StageModule() returns a new module-<random hex> directory made with
  CreateDirectoryW and writes <TITLE>.so with CreateFileW(CREATE_NEW,
  FILE_ATTRIBUTE_READONLY). POSIX keeps mkdtemp + O_EXCL. A failed stage
  removes its directory.
- OpenStaged() loads with LoadLibraryExW on the wide path (LoadLibraryA
  broke non-ASCII cache paths) or dlopen, and returns the loader's error
  text; the loader wraps the handle in Common::DynamicLibrary.
- RemoveStaged() clears the read-only attribute before remove_all, which
  Windows otherwise refuses; used by ~GameModule and SweepStale().

